-Preclinical data suggest that low-dose lithium orotate may aid recovery from traumatic brain injury by promoting neuronal survival and synaptogenesis. In TBI models, low-dose lithium mitigates oxidative damage and enhances cognitive rehabilitation, improving motor coordination and reducing long-term deficits through mechanisms including reduced apoptosis and increased synaptic plasticity [40]. These effects may partly involve BDNF upregulation. Human data on lithium for TBI are absent.
