-Most lithium toxicity is mild and includes lethargy, vomiting, difficulty with balance, and muscle tremors [1]. Larger doses or chronic use of high doses can cause coma or seizures (Pauze et al., *J Med Toxicol*, 2007) [47]. Serum lithium concentrations above 1.5 mEq/L are associated with toxicity risks including confusion, ataxia, and gastrointestinal distress — these levels are not achievable with typical low-dose supplements [2][3].
